---
import Site from '../../layouts/Site.astro';
import { u } from '../../lib/site';
---
<Site title={'LUMEN: Load, Usage & Management of Energy Networks'} description={'Power monitoring for GregTech: New Horizons: every LSC on one screen, switches and alerts.'} active="lumen">
<main>

<section aria-labelledby="hero" style="max-width: 1240px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 80px 24px 72px; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 56px; align-items: center">
<div style="flex: 1 1 420px; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 22px">
<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px">
<svg width="44" height="44" viewBox="0 0 44 44" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="2" y="14" width="40" height="16" rx="3" fill="#1C2229"/><rect x="2" y="14" width="29" height="16" rx="3" fill="#4FD17A"/><path d="M13 9 V35" stroke="#FFD24D" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-dasharray="2 3"/><path d="M38 9 V35" stroke="#FFD24D" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-dasharray="2 3"/></svg>
<span style="font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #8FE3AA">Load, Usage &amp; Management of Energy Networks</span>
</div>
<h1 id="hero" style="margin: 0; font-size: 56px; line-height: 1.05; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.025em">Know when the power runs out.<br><span style="color: #4FD17A">Before it does.</span></h1>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.6; color: #B7C0C9; max-width: 560px">Power monitoring for GregTech: New Horizons. LUMEN shows every Lapotronic Supercapacitor a computer reaches on one screen, with history and alerts that don't cry wolf. It shows your generators and IC2 reactors, and switches generators on and off with the LSCs' fill.</p>
<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; padding-top: 6px">
<a class="btn" href={u("lumen/docs/")} style="background: #4FD17A; color: #04170B">Read the docs <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a>
<a class="btn" href="https://github.com/aharabedian/lumen" style="background: #161B21; color: #E6EAEE; border: 1px solid #2A323B">aharabedian/lumen</a>
</div>
</div>
<figure style="flex: 1 1 560px; min-width: 0; margin: 0">
<div style="background: #0F1317; border: 1px solid #232A32; border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden">
<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; padding: 10px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid #1C2229; font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; color: #9AA5B1">
<span>lumen — 3 LSCs, 73.3% full</span>
<span style="color: #4FD17A">net +2.82k EU/t</span>
</div>
<img src={u("shots/lumen/lumen-three.png")} alt="LUMEN on a tier 3 screen: an All LSCs panel at 73.3 percent, Backup at 75 percent, Main at 95 percent with a history chart, Spare at 10 percent in red, and three alerts" style="display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 1280 / 800">
</div>
</figure>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="screen" style="border-top: 1px solid #1C2229; background: #0D1014">
<div style="max-width: 1240px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 88px 24px; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 48px; align-items: center">
<div style="flex: 1 1 400px; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px">
<p style="margin: 0; font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #9AA5B1">The screen</p>
<h2 id="screen" style="margin: 0; font-size: 38px; line-height: 1.12; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em">One panel per LSC. Tap for the last 24 hours.</h2>
<ul style="margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0; border-top: 1px solid #232A32">
<li style="display: flex; gap: 16px; padding: 12px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #1C2229; font-size: 15.5px; color: #C9D1D9"><span style="font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px; color: #4FD17A; width: 92px; flex: none; padding-top: 2px">fill</span>Stored and capacity EU, percentage full, and a bar that turns yellow or red with an alert</li>
<li style="display: flex; gap: 16px; padding: 12px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #1C2229; font-size: 15.5px; color: #C9D1D9"><span style="font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px; color: #4FD17A; width: 92px; flex: none; padding-top: 2px">flows</span>EU/t in, out and net; the net over 5 minutes and over 1 hour</li>
<li style="display: flex; gap: 16px; padding: 12px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #1C2229; font-size: 15.5px; color: #C9D1D9"><span style="font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px; color: #4FD17A; width: 92px; flex: none; padding-top: 2px">time</span>Time to full or empty, as the LSC itself works it out</li>
<li style="display: flex; gap: 16px; padding: 12px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #1C2229; font-size: 15.5px; color: #C9D1D9"><span style="font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px; color: #4FD17A; width: 92px; flex: none; padding-top: 2px">history</span>Fill over 80 min, 8 h or 24 h, surviving a restart</li>
<li style="display: flex; gap: 16px; padding: 12px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #1C2229; font-size: 15.5px; color: #C9D1D9"><span style="font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px; color: #4FD17A; width: 92px; flex: none; padding-top: 2px">last 24 h</span>EU in and out, peak draw and when, lowest fill, how long each switch was on, against the day before</li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure style="flex: 1 1 540px; min-width: 0; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px">
<img src={u("shots/lumen/lumen-detail.png")} alt="An LSC's detail page: fill history over 8 hours, EU/t averages over 5 seconds, 5 minutes and 1 hour, and the last 24 hours" style="display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 1280 / 800; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid #232A32">
<figcaption style="font-size: 13.5px; color: #9AA5B1">An LSC's own page, 8 H range.</figcaption>
</figure>
</div>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="switches" style="border-top: 1px solid #1C2229">
<div style="max-width: 1240px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 88px 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 44px">
<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 20px 64px; align-items: flex-end">
<div style="flex: 1 1 440px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
<p style="margin: 0; font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #9AA5B1">Switches</p>
<h2 id="switches" style="margin: 0; font-size: 38px; line-height: 1.12; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em">Generators on when you need them. No flicker.</h2>
</div>
<p style="flex: 1 1 380px; margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.65; color: #B7C0C9">A switch turns generators on below one mark and off above another, and leaves them alone in between. By redstone signal, or through a GT machine's work switch.</p>
</div>

<div style="background: #0F1317; border: 1px solid #232A32; border-radius: 14px; padding: 32px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px">
<div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 12.5px; color: #9AA5B1"><span>0%</span><span>LSC fill</span><span>100%</span></div>
<div style="display: flex; height: 64px; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden">
<div style="flex: 30; background: #13281B; border-right: 2px dashed #FFD24D; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; padding: 0 8px"><span style="font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #4FD17A; text-align: center">turn ON</span></div>
<div style="flex: 60; background: #161B21; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; padding: 0 8px"><span style="font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; color: #AEB8C2; text-align: center">leave it alone</span></div>
<div style="flex: 10; background: #2A1416; border-left: 2px dashed #FFD24D; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; padding: 0 4px"><span style="font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #FF8A8A">OFF</span></div>
</div>
<div style="display: flex; font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px; color: #FFD24D"><span style="flex: 30; text-align: right; padding-right: 4px">onBelow = 30</span><span style="flex: 60"></span><span style="flex: 10; text-align: left; white-space: nowrap; transform: translateX(-100%)">offAbove = 90</span></div>
</div>

<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr)); gap: 28px 40px">
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; padding-top: 18px; border-top: 1px solid #232A32"><h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600">A restart never flips anything</h3><p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #B7C0C9">At start LUMEN reads the output as it is. It waits a minute between switches, and holds while it can't read the LSCs.</p></div>
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; padding-top: 18px; border-top: 1px solid #232A32"><h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600">You can always take over</h3><p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #B7C0C9">ON and OFF on the screen override the switch, kept across restarts, until you tap AUTO.</p></div>
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; padding-top: 18px; border-top: 1px solid #232A32"><h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600">Alerts know about switches</h3><p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #B7C0C9">Draining while the generators are off is expected: the panel says <em>standby</em>. Once they've run 10 minutes, a drain alert means "on, and still not keeping up".</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="scope" style="border-top: 1px solid #1C2229; background: #0D1014">
<div style="max-width: 1240px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 88px 24px; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 48px; align-items: flex-start">
<div style="flex: 1 1 360px; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px">
<p style="margin: 0; font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #9AA5B1">Scope</p>
<h2 id="scope" style="margin: 0; font-size: 38px; line-height: 1.12; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em">Simple, safe control. On purpose.</h2>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.65; color: #B7C0C9">A computer polling every few seconds is great at watching and at slow, safe decisions. It isn't a reactor controller, and LUMEN doesn't pretend to be one.</p>
<img src={u("shots/lumen/lumen-control.png")} alt="LUMEN with a vacuum reactor on a switch, showing the POWER section with AUTO, ON and OFF buttons" style="display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 1280 / 800; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid #232A32; margin-top: 8px">
</div>
<div style="flex: 1 1 520px; min-width: 0; border: 1px solid #232A32; border-radius: 12px; overflow-x: auto">
<table class="t">
<thead><tr><th style="color: #4FD17A">In</th><th style="color: #FF8A8A">Out</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Reading LSCs and other GT energy storage: stored EU, input, output, time to full or empty</td><td><strong style="color: #E6EAEE">Automated reactor control.</strong> OpenComputers can't swap reactor components atomically; a mod built for it (Steve's Factory Manager) does it better</td></tr>
<tr><td>Switching generators on and off with the LSC's fill</td><td>Anything that needs reactions faster than a computer polling every few seconds</td></tr>
<tr><td>Alerts for low power and draining fast, and reporting to <a href={u("lens/")} style="color: #8CCBFF">LENS</a></td><td></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="start" style="border-top: 1px solid #1C2229">
<div style="max-width: 1240px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 88px 24px; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 48px">
<div style="flex: 1 1 440px; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px">
<h2 id="start" style="margin: 0; font-size: 34px; line-height: 1.15; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em">Quick start</h2>
<pre class="code"><span class="p">$</span> wget -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aharabedian/lumen/main/src/lumen-update.lua /home/lumen-update.lua
<span class="p">$</span> /home/lumen-update
<span class="p">$</span> lumen-setup
<span class="p">$</span> lumen</pre>
<div style="border: 1px solid #232A32; border-radius: 10px; overflow-x: auto">
<table class="t">
<thead><tr><th>Program</th><th>Does</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><code class="i">lumen</code></td><td>The power screen, switches and alerts; reports to LENS</td></tr>
<tr><td><code class="i">lumen-setup</code></td><td>Asks about LSCs, generators, switches, alerts and LENS; writes <code class="i">/home/lumen.cfg</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code class="i">lumen-discover</code></td><td>Lists components; <code class="i">--read</code> shows what an LSC reports</td></tr>
<tr><td><code class="i">lumen-update</code></td><td>Installs and updates LUMEN</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div style="flex: 1 1 440px; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px">
<h2 style="margin: 0; font-size: 34px; line-height: 1.15; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em">What you need</h2>
<ul style="margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; border: 1px solid #232A32; border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden">
<li style="padding: 14px 18px; border-bottom: 1px solid #1C2229; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.55; color: #C9D1D9"><strong style="color: #E6EAEE">A computer</strong> (tier 2 or better) with a GPU and screen. Tier 3 gives the full layout</li>
<li style="padding: 14px 18px; border-bottom: 1px solid #1C2229; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.55; color: #C9D1D9"><strong style="color: #E6EAEE">An adapter</strong> on each LSC's controller block</li>
<li style="padding: 14px 18px; border-bottom: 1px solid #1C2229; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.55; color: #C9D1D9"><strong style="color: #E6EAEE">Optional:</strong> adapters on generators, a Redstone I/O block for switches, a network card for LENS</li>
<li style="padding: 14px 18px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.55; color: #C9D1D9"><strong style="color: #E6EAEE">An Internet Card</strong> to install and update. Take it out afterwards</li>
</ul>
<figure style="margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px"><img src={u("shots/lumen/lumen-tier2.png")} alt="LUMEN on a tier 2 screen with the essentials of each panel" style="display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 420px; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 640 / 400; border-radius: 10px; border: 1px solid #232A32"><figcaption style="font-size: 13.5px; color: #9AA5B1">Tier 2 keeps the essentials.</figcaption></figure>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section aria-label="Part of the suite" style="border-top: 1px solid #1C2229; background: #0D1014">
<div style="max-width: 1240px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 56px 24px; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 20px 40px; align-items: center">
<p style="flex: 1 1 480px; margin: 0; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; color: #C9D1D9">A sibling of <a href={u("prism/")} style="color: #FFB86B">PRISM</a> and <a href={u("lens/")} style="color: #8CCBFF">LENS</a>. Report to a hub and see power next to your ore line, or in your glasses.</p>
<a class="btn" href={u("guide/")} style="background: #161B21; color: #E6EAEE; border: 1px solid #2A323B">Putting the suite together</a>
</div>
</section>

</main>
</Site>
